          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A weighted colimit (also called
            %em indexed colimit
            or
            %em mean tensor product
            in older texts) is a concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            suitable for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
          %h2#motivation Motivation
          %p
            Recall that a colimit of a diagram in a category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: J \to C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %strong cocone
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is a natural transformation from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            to a constant diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(c) = (J \to 1 \stackrel{c}{\to} C)
          %p
            so that a cocone for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is an object of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \downarrow \Delta
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta: C^1 \to C^J
            is the diagonal functor obtained by pulling back along the unique functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \to 1
            %strong universal cocone
            is simply an initial object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \downarrow \Delta
          %p
            In enriched category theory, where one considers categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            enriched in a “nice”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            (generally one where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta: C \to C^J
            to speak of. For example, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is the category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \simeq C^I
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is the unit
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            for which
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(1, 1) = \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} Ab-enriched category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \to I
            to pull back along (or, there may be many, but none stand out as canonical). This shows that the usual notion of colimit doesn’t adapt particularly well to the general enriched setting.
          %p
            The more flexible notion of weighted colimit (also called an
            %em indexed colimit
            in some of the older accounts) was introduced by Borceux (and Kelly?) as giving the
            %em right
            notion of colimit for enriched category theory.
          %h2#weighted_colimits_in_ordinary_category_theory Weighted colimits in ordinary category theory
          %p
            First we reformulate ordinary colimits in the language of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
          %p
            Assume for the moment that the receiving category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has all
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has all colimits; the proof is we can write down a formula for the colimit of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: J \to C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mi J
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{j, k \in Ob(J)} hom(j, k) \times F(j) \overset{\to}{\to} \sum_{k \in Ob(J)} F(k) \to colim_J F
          %p
            where the cartesian product on the left refers to a coproduct of copies of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(j)
            indexed over the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(j, k)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(j, k) \times F(j) \to F(k) = \langle F(f): F(j) \to F(k) \rangle_{f: j \to k}
          %p and the other is induced by a collection of projections
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(j, k) \times F(j) \to F(j)
          %p
            each of which is the application of the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \times F(j): Set \to C
            to the unique map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo !
                  %mo :
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !: hom(j, k) \to 1.
          %p
            We can think of the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(j, k) \to 1
            also as a component of an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            acts on the terminal functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1: J \to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            acts covariantly on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            (so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is a
            %em left
            = succeed "-module)," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            acting
            %em contravariantly
            on the terminal functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1: J \to Set
            (so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            becomes a
            %em right
            = succeed "-module)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            Then the colimit of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            above is precisely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of the left module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            with the right module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi j
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{j, k} 1(k) \times hom(j, k) \times F(j) \overset{\to}{\to} \sum_j 1(j) \times F(j)
          %p
            where one arrow is induced from a right action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            on the functor 1, having components
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_{j, k} \times F(j): (1(k) \times hom(j, k)) \times F(j) \to 1(j) \times F(j)
          %p
            and the other is induced from a left action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1(k) \times \lambda_{j, k}: 1(k) \times (hom(j, k) \times F(j)) \to 1(k) \times F(k)
          %p
            From this standpoint, the colimit of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is a rather specialized tensor product of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi J
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \otimes_J F
          %p
            and the unsuitability of this notion for general enriched categories could be thought of as a case of putting all one’s eggs in the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            basket.
          %p
            A general right
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W: J^{op} \to Set
            may be called a
            %strong weight
            (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(j)
            the weight at
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            an equal weight
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(j) = 1
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W: J^{op} \to Set
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %em weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: J \to C
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %em diagram
            %strong weighted colimit
            or tensor product is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W * F
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            together with an isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(W * F, c) \cong Set^{J^{op}}(W, C(F-, c))
          %p
            that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural
            in objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(j) \to C(F(j), W * F),
          %p
            natural in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
          %p
            The notion of weighted colimit carries over in straightforward fashion to categories enriched in a complete, cocomplete, closed symmetric monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is a small
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: J \to C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W: J^{op} \to V
            are
            = succeed "-functors," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            with respect to the weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W * F
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            together with an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+natural+transformation"} natural
            isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(W * F, c) \cong V^{J^{op}}(W, C(F-, c))
          %p
            (between
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be complete, cocomplete, and closed, at the cost of not being able to refer to functor categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi J
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{J^{op}}
          %p
            A leitmotif playing in the background is that the category of weights
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{J^{op}}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            (or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{J^{op}}
            in the enriched case) is the free (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            \-enriched) cocompletion of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            \-)category which is cocomplete in the “right” sense of the word, then every (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            \-)functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: J \to C
            extends, uniquely up to unique (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            \-)isomorphism, to a (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            \-)cocontinuous functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo ˜
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{F}: V^{J^{op}} \to C
          %p
            which is given by the weighted colimit construction
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \mapsto W * F
          %p
            Weighted colimits are covariantly functorial in both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi W
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \Rightarrow W'
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi F
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \Rightarrow F'
            induces a morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                    %mo ′
                    %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W * F \to W' * F'
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conical+colimit"} conical colimit
                is a weighted colimit where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(j)=I
                (the monoidal unit of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(j)=1
                in the case
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo =
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is the diagram.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
                is a weighted colimit where
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J=1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                picks out the object of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                picks out the object of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+functors"} tensor product of functors
                is a general example.
          %h2#cocompleteness Cocompleteness
          %p
            An enriched category admits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            if it admits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conical+colimits"} conical colimits
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coends"} coends
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W: J^{op} \to Set
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: J \to C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W * F \cong \int^{j \in J} W(j) \cdot F(j)
          %p Thus a category with all conical colimits and copowers is cocomplete.
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+weighted+colimit"} homotopy weighted colimit
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              Very nice descriptions on the n-Cafe by:
              %ul
                %li
